{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25599690",
      "title": "What & Why",
      "sourceHash": "92d51cd55a653964cc4103b9bcc0bef8a819f21cefdd0610be12e36368ca3293",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.24,
          "end": 3.31,
          "en": "Now as I mentioned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.31,
          "end": 5.52,
          "en": "in the last lecture already,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.52,
          "end": 8.01,
          "en": "Class-Based Components exist",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.01,
          "end": 11.63,
          "en": "and they are an alternative to functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.63,
          "end": 14.22,
          "en": "Up to this point, when we built Components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.22,
          "end": 16.53,
          "en": "they looked something like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.53,
          "end": 19,
          "en": "Of course, instead of the function keyword,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19,
          "end": 20.51,
          "en": "we might have used const",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 20.51,
          "end": 23.11,
          "en": "and stored an arrow function in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 23.11,
          "end": 26.7,
          "en": "But either way, we simply built a function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 26.7,
          "end": 27.78,
          "en": "That is what we did.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 27.78,
          "end": 31.2,
          "en": "And we built a function that receives props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 31.2,
          "end": 34.1,
          "en": "and then returns the JSX code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 34.1,
          "end": 36.283,
          "en": "that should be rendered to the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 37.21,
          "end": 40.06,
          "en": "This is what Components are in React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 40.06,
          "end": 43.55,
          "en": "and they are simply regular JavaScript functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 43.55,
          "end": 47.93,
          "en": "which return some renderable results, typically JSX.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 47.93,
          "end": 52.64,
          "en": "This is what we refer to as Functional Components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.64,
          "end": 56.65,
          "en": "which is a term I also already used a couple of times.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 56.65,
          "end": 58.16,
          "en": "Now this term exists",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.16,
          "end": 61.53,
          "en": "because it's not the only way of building Components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 61.53,
          "end": 63.1,
          "en": "If it would be the only way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 63.1,
          "end": 66.54,
          "en": "we could just call it Components, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 66.54,
          "end": 69.28,
          "en": "But we call it Functional Components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 69.28,
          "end": 73.65,
          "en": "because there is an alternative way of defining Components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 73.65,
          "end": 75.5,
          "en": "Not of using them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 75.5,
          "end": 79.55,
          "en": "You always use them as custom HTML elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 79.55,
          "end": 81.03999999999999,
          "en": "in your JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 81.03999999999999,
          "end": 84.82300000000001,
          "en": "But for defining them, there is this alternative.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 85.7,
          "end": 90.7,
          "en": "You can define a Component by creating a class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.83,
          "end": 94.31,
          "en": "which is a default JavaScript feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 94.31,
          "end": 96.84,
          "en": "Classes are not a React feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 96.84,
          "end": 100.41,
          "en": "classes exist in modern JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 100.41,
          "end": 104.31,
          "en": "And you can define a class with a render method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 104.31,
          "end": 106.88,
          "en": "and that is a reserved name, render.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 106.88,
          "end": 108.35,
          "en": "It has to be named like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 108.35,
          "end": 111.8,
          "en": "And then React will call that render method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 111.8,
          "end": 115.85,
          "en": "to evaluate what should be rendered to the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 115.85,
          "end": 120.14,
          "en": "So this is an alternative way of defining Components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 120.14,
          "end": 124.53,
          "en": "And that is what is referred to as class Components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 124.53,
          "end": 127.163,
          "en": "or Class-Based Components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 128.23,
          "end": 132.35,
          "en": "Now, I will emphasize the left approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 132.35,
          "end": 134.74,
          "en": "using Functional Components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 134.74,
          "end": 138.09,
          "en": "is the default and most modern approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 138.09,
          "end": 140.32,
          "en": "of building Components these days.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 140.32,
          "end": 144.39,
          "en": "And in most modern React projects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 144.39,
          "end": 146.21,
          "en": "you will therefore pretty much",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 146.21,
          "end": 149.52,
          "en": "work with Functional Components only.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 149.52,
          "end": 153.13,
          "en": "You might never build a single class-based Component there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 153.13,
          "end": 157.04,
          "en": "because nowadays with the exception of error boundaries,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 157.04,
          "end": 158.81,
          "en": "which we'll have a look at later,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 158.81,
          "end": 163.11,
          "en": "there is no reason to go for Class-Based Components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 163.11,
          "end": 165.86,
          "en": "Except for personal preferences, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 165.86,
          "end": 169.12,
          "en": "You can simply prefer Class-Based Components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 169.12,
          "end": 172.04,
          "en": "and that would be absolutely fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 172.04,
          "end": 173.79,
          "en": "You can build anything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 173.79,
          "end": 176.57,
          "en": "you can build with Functional Components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 176.57,
          "end": 179.36,
          "en": "with Class-Based Components as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 179.36,
          "end": 182.57,
          "en": "It just requires a different mental model",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 182.57,
          "end": 185.81,
          "en": "in some regards and some aspects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 185.81,
          "end": 188.67,
          "en": "Now, the Class-Based Components exist",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 188.67,
          "end": 192.12,
          "en": "because they were required in the past.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 192.12,
          "end": 197.12,
          "en": "In the past, which means prior to React 16.8,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 197.71,
          "end": 201.39,
          "en": "there were scenarios and use cases",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 201.39,
          "end": 204.72,
          "en": "where you needed Class-Based Components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 204.72,
          "end": 208.09,
          "en": "Specifically when dealing with State",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 208.09,
          "end": 210.52,
          "en": "and with side effects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 210.52,
          "end": 214.03,
          "en": "you had to use Class-Based Components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 214.03,
          "end": 217.74,
          "en": "Traditionally, prior to React 16.8,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 217.74,
          "end": 221.8,
          "en": "you could not change State in Functional Components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 221.8,
          "end": 225.303,
          "en": "and you couldn't really handle side effects there either.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 226.34,
          "end": 229.52,
          "en": "That changed with React 16.8",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 229.52,
          "end": 231.21,
          "en": "because that React version",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 231.21,
          "end": 234.78,
          "en": "introduced a concept called React Hooks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 234.78,
          "end": 236.79,
          "en": "which are all these Hooks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 236.79,
          "end": 239.22,
          "en": "these functions starting with use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 239.22,
          "end": 243.28,
          "en": "UseState and useEffect and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 243.28,
          "end": 247.07,
          "en": "These are functions for Functional Components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 247.07,
          "end": 250.73,
          "en": "which bring features to Functional Components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 250.73,
          "end": 255.13,
          "en": "which previously were reserved for Class-Based Components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 255.13,
          "end": 259.87,
          "en": "And indeed, Class-Based Components can't use React Hooks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 259.87,
          "end": 261.54,
          "en": "That's also important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 261.54,
          "end": 263.83,
          "en": "That's really important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 263.83,
          "end": 266.98,
          "en": "What you learned about react Hooks up to this point,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 266.98,
          "end": 269.45,
          "en": "it does not matter at all",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 269.45,
          "end": 272.68,
          "en": "when working with Class-Based Components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 272.68,
          "end": 274.69,
          "en": "But now in the next lectures,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 274.69,
          "end": 277.15,
          "en": "I'll show you how you can convert",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 277.15,
          "end": 280.25,
          "en": "Functional Components to Class-Based Components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 280.25,
          "end": 282.44,
          "en": "how you can manage State there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 282.44,
          "end": 286.18,
          "en": "and also how you translate useEffect and useContext",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 287.317,
          "end": 290.943,
          "en": "and useReducer to the Class-Based Component world.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}